From: A. Donz <Avrova@Donz.si>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] compiler: allow using the packaged nanobind source

Upstream-Status: Downstream (openRuyi packaging; avoids network access during build)
Upstream-Reference: https://github.com/iree-org/iree/blob/v3.8.0/compiler/setup.py

The compiler build obtains nanobind through CMake FetchContent. Let the source
RPM provide the exact pinned nanobind source tree instead.

--- a/compiler/setup.py
+++ b/compiler/setup.py
@@ -271,6 +271,12 @@
             get_env_cmake_option("IREE_TARGET_BACKEND_CUDA", "OFF"),
             get_env_cmake_option("IREE_ENABLE_LLD", "OFF"),
+            get_env_cmake_option("IREE_BUILD_BUNDLED_LLVM", "OFF"),
         ]
+        nanobind_source_dir = os.getenv("IREE_NANOBIND_SOURCE_DIR")
+        if nanobind_source_dir:
+            cmake_args.append(
+                f"-DFETCHCONTENT_SOURCE_DIR_NANOBIND={nanobind_source_dir}"
+            )
         cmake_args.extend(get_cmake_version_info_args())
